# Figure 32 Author Observations

Status: FIGURE_AUTHORED_NOT_APPROVED.

Scope: finite ld-s10y-image cap1 + cap2 author work for NEW8a / alg8-c3-s3-n20 / exercise 320 only. No cap4, review@1, promotion, lesson-manifest edit, answer work, choice work or solving.

## Independent Original Inventory

Opened the durable original `8a/figures/fig-32.png` once at its complete 599 x 576 pixel detail, without crops or resizes. Inventory was established from these pixels before creating the spec and is retained in `inventory.json`.

One shared Oxy coordinate frame contains filled B(1,2), A(3,5), C(6,1), solid BA and BC, and dashed vertical projections ending on the x axis at 1,3,6. There is no AC edge and no full grid. The horizontal axis has unit ticks 1 through 7; the vertical axis has unit ticks 1 through 6. Both axes print only 2,4,6, have positive arrowheads and short negative tails. O, A, B, C, x and y are the instructional labels. Isolated scan flecks are not objects.

The prepared prose names the broken line ABC. That wording was not used to infer an absent AC edge or to change the independently observed source geometry.

Modern layout adjustments are limited to clean strokes, readable Latin mathematical labels, neutral semantic colors, regularized blank axis extensions and balanced canvas margins. They are declared separately from source facts.

## Prepared Text Context

`context.json` contains the full prepared lesson and exercise files, their embedded source data and source SHA bindings, and the complete relevant lesson prose plus exercise 320 in `authoritativeText`. It explicitly identifies itself as draft prepared-text context, not durable final-edition context. `build_context.py` was not run.

Another author's text normalization changed the prepared lesson/exercise files while this work was starting. Two preparation attempts stopped on SHA mismatches before creating context/spec; both receipts are retained. The recovery captured each prepared file into a single buffer and hashed those same bytes, rather than repeatedly chasing mutable input hashes. The captured complete text was read before rendering, and mathematical tokens were checked against embedded source text without solving any exercise.

Parent must bind the final authored text before releasing the independent figure gate. This author's captured draft text is not an independent text approval.

## Native Validation And Rendering

The spec uses the existing JSXGraph renderer, 15 objects and 19 native assertions. Exact source coordinates, BA/BC displacements, semantic segment endpoints, three projection endpoints, projection perpendicularity, an orthogonal frame, point/axis counts and absence of a full grid are asserted. Both source-point inventory groups require pointRelationships and map all three points to relationships wholly inside their group.

Initial draft validation passed. Native render attempt 1 exited 2 for point-label clearances at B, A and C. The original spec, SVG and failed render report are preserved in `receipts/render-0001/`; the original render receipt and stderr remain unchanged. Only label offsets were changed. The updated draft validation and render attempt 2 passed. There was no manual edit to renderer output.

## Actual 640 Pixel Preview

The saved actual SVG was displayed in the current product CSS figure classes with instructional scroll layout. Media and SVG measured 640 x 560 px, minimum final text measured 22 px, all twelve labels fit, and exact rendered point/segment/tick coordinates matched the shared equal-unit frame. At viewport 390 px the 358 px figure container retained 640 px media and reached horizontal scroll end 282 px. This is an offline product-CSS harness, not a fully bound durable lesson or full-product acceptance.

Opened only the complete 640 x 560 preview PNG, once. Author observation: nonblank output, clear filled markers, solid BA/BC, three visibly dashed vertical guides, readable labels and unit ticks, intact right/up arrowheads, small negative tails and clear diagram bounds. No AC edge, background grid, coordinate annotations or answer annotations. These are author observations, not independent approval.

The initial preview's non-asserted arrowhead statistic used the wrong DOM attribute and reported zero. A separate affected-only DOM check verified the unchanged SVG's two semantic arrowhead groups, then corrected that field. The original preview report is archived and the correction evidence is retained. The successful preview stage, raster screenshot and source inventory were not repeated.

